<title>JAPAN: Nippon Oil 1997 topper turnaround plans.</title>
<headline>Nippon Oil 1997 topper turnaround plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Nippon Oil Co Ltd's plans for routine maintenance closures of crude distillation units (CDU) in 1997 is as follows (capacity in barrels-per-day):</p>
<p>    Negishi 1		 120,000	 September to October</p>
<p>    Negishi 2		  70,000	 none</p>
<p>    Negishi 3		  55,000	 none</p>
<p>    Negishi 4		 140,000	 none</p>
<p>    Niigata		    26,000	 none</p>
<p>    Muroran		   170,000	 May to June</p>
<p>    Toyama		     60,000	 May to June</p>
<p>(The Toyama unit is owned by Nippon Oil's subsidiary Nihonkai Oil Co Ltd)</p>
</text>
